Maybe this should be added in the Nethcak myths. I've seen posted 
several times that a wizard has not enough skill poiints to advance all 
categories to personal max. This is not true.

It takes 1 skill point to advance from unskilled to basic or from basic 
to skilled. 2 points to advance from skilled to expert.

For wizard here is the chart on all spell categories:

Catergory     Start      End    Slots needed
---------------------------------------------
Attack        basic      expert      3
Healing       unskilled  skilled     2
Divination    unskilled  expert      4
Enchantment   basic      skilled     1
Clerical      unskilled  skilled     2
Escape        unskilled  expert      4
Matter        unskilled  expert      4
---------------------------------------------
Total                               20

As for a 30-level character there is 29 skill slots to distibute this 
leaves plenty to get dagger to max.

